26-10-21T18:56:39.273815+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Stage 5b: squint (input-conditioned adaptation)\n","The network reads the perturbation it is given: a gate head on the stem features predicts which threat it is looking at, and every BatchNorm affine is a gate-weighted mixture of per-threat parameters. `squint_v0` supervises the gate, `squint_v0_nogate` is the ablation. The compare point is `v3a_max` (same architecture without the gate). Evaluation attacks the whole gated system at the fixed ε. The gate's accuracy on the training attacks is in `log.jsonl` as `gate_acc`. The squint numbers to report are the **gate-aware adaptive** ones (`eval_adaptive.json`): the gate is attacked with forced routing and a temperature-softened softmax, and a point must survive all of them, because a saturated gate can hide weak spots from plain APGD. `v3a_max` is evaluated the same way with the same number of extra attacks, so compare squint's adaptive numbers with that matched baseline, in the same table (`--tag adaptive`). One seed first (about 1 h of training, two runs in parallel), then about 1.2 h of adaptive evaluation."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":14,"id":"2e575365","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-21T18:56:39.290692Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-21T18:56:39.290001Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-21T18:56:44.231671Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-21T18:56:44.230996Z"},"papermill":{"duration":4.948882,"end_time":"2026-10-21T18:56:44.233156+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-21T18:56:39.284274+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"model_id":"8b6be968f637405ca52a82658514db3b","version_major":2,"version_minor":0},"text/plain":["aat/squint_v0_s0/final.pt:   0%|          | 0.00/44.9M [00:00<?, ?B/s]"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[hub] pulled aat/squint_v0_s0/final.pt <- matokebr